Apollo 16 Soil Mechanics                                                      
Lunar Self-Recording Penetrometer (LSRP) Page D-1                             
                                                                              
Plot of Pre-Flight Load Calibration Tests                                     
                                                                              
This handdrawn plot shows the drum circumferential deflection in              
millimeters versus the load in Newtons for PDA/drum S/N 2003 of the           
Apollo 16 Lunar Self-Recording Penetrometer (LSRP) flight unit. A series      
of 12 calibration tests were run and form a straight line. The load in        
Newtons (ordinate) is labelled from 0 to 200 newtons, and the drum            
circumferential deflection (abscissa) is labelled from 0 to 15                
millimeters.                                                                  
